ng  uh turn the channel and get into  something different because  it was a tough one to watch we had such  a great year and and it was such a crazy  year with  the pandemic and all the rules and  restrictions and our guys certainly  um overcame a lot of hurdles and you  know best  record in franchise history 14-2 um had  a really good performance against  buffalo in the ac championship game and  unfortunately this league is is you say  it every year it's a battle of attrition  and you know we were just some bodies  short and now that's taking nothing away  from tampa they played an unbelievable  game they were hot at the right time  they were healthy  you're hot and healthy in those playoffs  it's tough and a couple years ago we got  hot and healthy and and  you know we were able to finish the deal  and and this year we just  came a little bit short on the healthy  side of things and and hopefully  the work that we've done this offseason  the depth we build on on both the  offensive defense line will  help us survive a 17-game schedule  what was the number one thing though  that stood out to you when you watched  the game that that is relevant to your  job what do i need to do  to help us avoid an outcome like this  based upon what you saw in super bowl 55  what's that one thing that stood out  listen i think it just reinforces things  that you know we're already aware of and  it is just  a it's a battle of attrition i mean you  know  listen it we didn't have both starting  tackles and um we had an offensive guard  get hurt earlier in the season and we  had two players opt out so you know we  were  we were shorthanded to begin with but  the reality of it is every team  has the same scenarios they have to play  and and every year teams  lose players and it's our responsibility  in our job to make sure that  the roster is deep but on top of that  that your practice squad is always  uh deep and healthy and competitive  because it's interesting i mean you can  look at 