d and continue to get him  weapons but um it's certainly  an exciting feeling for us for our  organization for our city to know that  um you know when the game's kicked off  on sunday that number 15 is our  quarterback  hey last thing for you and and i have to  say thank you for giving us  a nice little area of news  and developments and everything  associated that comes from that  revolutionary change to the numbering  system that the chiefs proposed  and and and i know the basic reason was  we ran out of numbers last year  but after the rule went through brett  tom brady started complaining about it i  don't know why i didn't complain about  it ahead of time maybe he didn't know  but what do you understand his concern  to be and do  do you think there's any merit to his  belief that it's a dumb  change to allow so many guys to wear  single digits and linebackers to wear  one all the way up to 49.  well i mean 59. yeah no i mean listen  there's certainly always varying  opinions especially when you make role  changes to things that have been in  place for for such a long time and  they're certainly  traditionalists and and listen i had a  long conversation with clark  uh before working with this we were just  in this unique  situation where we have a bunch of  retired numbers i think we have 12 or 13  members retired 10 of which are skilled  players  last year we had 16 players on the  practice squad we had the ability to  flex these players up and down  and we were just literally running out  of of numbers uh to give  defensive backs receivers and really it  was just a need for us we just needed  the ability with the expanded rosters  and expanded practice squads and flexing  people up and down just  more flexibility from numbers i think  the one we had three players wearing  number 30 out there in the practice  field and  i kind of said to our equipment manager  i said man we just we you know we have  to do this if college can do it why  can't we do it i mean col